    dict(key='19-act-6-figure', kind='figure', title='The probes, round by round',
         body='probe_rounds',
         narration='Sixth demo: does anybody hear it? [[slnc 400]] A control that fails closed still needs someone to be told, or the bank only finds out from angry customers. [[slnc 600]] At the top, the probes during the authorization outage. [[slnc 300]] Each round, the monitor asks the health endpoint. [[slnc 300]] Round one fails, then round two, then round three: three in a row, and that raises one alert. [[slnc 300]] Round four fails too, but the alert is already out. [[slnc 700]] In the middle, the slow close of the audit sink. [[slnc 300]] Every probe is answered, so there is no alert, and that is right: a slow close costs nothing. [[slnc 600]] Counting in probes, not seconds, keeps the result the same on every machine.'),
